SSSTRAVELTIME
+++++++++++++

SUMMARY
-------
Computes traveltime of selected phases for pre-defined velocity models
Description and examples assume the calls are made from within SSS.
The source file is the same as the non-SSS version, and this file has
only an example that uses SSS plotting.  For the full description, see
TRAVELTIME_.

EXAMPLE
-------
The point of this example is to demonstrate how PLOTRECORDSECTION_ can
be used with TRAVELTIME.  A difference between PRS and P1_ is that for
P1, the plot order from top-to-bottom depends on the order the waveforms
are read in.  We use the same data set and traveltime runs as in
TRAVELTIME_, but PRS automatically orders the waveforms by distance,

If one first goes into SSS and then does the datagen command, the prs plot
will have the lines for the arrivals but no waveforms or labeled picks.

Unlike the plot for *P1* in TRAVELTIME_, the aspect ratio is such that save to
PDF has some errors.

PRS* does not work for distance in kilometers::

     SAC> datagen sub deep  bla.r kev.r kip.r pas.r ; rtr
     SAC> SSS
     SAC/SSS> traveltime quiet picks 0 phase sPP
     SAC/SSS> traveltime  quiet picks 1 phase P pP sP S sS SKS
     SAC/SSS> dw units degrees fixed 50 90 ;  tw 400 1500
     SAC/SSS> prs orient port ttime on labels kstcmp
     SAC/SSS> save sakhalin-picks-prs.xpm

